if you guys are regular viewers of our  channel you will already know that we  come out with tons of elon and tesla  videos this is because we absolutely  love what that man is doing with his  super successful car brand and we truly  believe that tesla will be a global  powerhouse very soon so here we are back  at it again with another video on elon  musk and tesla if you are also impressed  by elon at some level you will want to  stick around as we are going to discuss  something very juicy in this video do me  a favor look back a decade did you ever  imagine that self-driving cars would be  a reality on our roads or that humanity  could possibly consider taking a trip to  mars in another few years i don't think  any of us did well we all know about  spacex's mars mission but did you know  that elon and tesla just made another  giant stride in the field of  self-driving cars with their new  partnership with samsung today we will  explore that new partnership with  samsung which will be manufacturing  tesla's new self-driving chip and why  this has the potential of being another  game changer we all know that tesla's  autopilot technology is still one of the  best in its class it is a system that  has been developed and thoroughly user  tested in commercial models but over the  last few years other manufacturers have  slowly caught up to it many other car  companies have started following tesla's  example and started dabbling in this  space with launches such as the infiniti  qx50 or the kia k5 these car companies  have not only given intense competition  to tesla but also managed to improve on  certain self-driving technology so with  this new samsung deal elon and the  engineers at tesla are planning for  another quantum leap that will allow  them to outperform their rivals once  again as you'll discover over the course  of this video this is something that is  years in the making and if it goes  according to elon's plan then fully  self-driving cars will be a reality in  just a few more years elon first  announced this in 2019 at an investor  conference and since then work has begun  between the two companies to get the new  hw 4.0 chip and its associated systems  ready by 2022. although it is not  confirmed yet the new hw 4.0 chip is  widely expected to be introduced in the  tesla cyber truck which will begin  delivery in late 2022 so what is this  new chip all about and how can switching  to a new chip manufacturer help tesla  let us explore tesla cars were the first  to include the autopilot feature in its  commercial models all the way back in  2014. in those days autopilot relied on  a series of cameras and radar technology  to process its surroundings all of the  gathered data was fed into tesla's  proprietary computer vision software  which then used a chip inside the car's  computer to do all the heavy  calculations keeping your car within the  white lines of the highway but after  seven strong years of development and  user testing autopilot technology has  advanced leaps and bounds the system has  become so efficient that tesla announced  in its 2021 ai day that it is dropping  the radar altogether instead the new  tesla vision system will utilize just  cameras and an ai neural net to keep the  cars on track bringing us ever closer to  the promise of fully self-driving cars  what is a neural net you wonder well  simply put it's a hive mind of  artificial intelligence the idea is to  reflect the behavior of the human brain  allowing computer programs to recognize  patterns and solve problems using ai and  machine learning for its cars tesla is  in the process of developing a neural  net that when trained and scaled up  properly can predict all types of  driving scenarios make split-second  decisions based on road and traffic  conditions and constantly learn to  improve itself over time this massive  undertaking was made possible due to a  lawn development process inside tesla  that has as much to do with the software  side of things as it is to do with the  rapid development of chips capable of  training the ai and running those  massive calculations in split seconds  and this is where the new partnership  with samsung comes in from the very  beginning of the company elon has stated  his vision of creating totally  self-driving vehicles and has moved  stridently to innovate in this field of  ai so since 2016 tesla has been pouring  resources into its own in-house r d team  for neural net development and chip  making this led to the development of  its first fully self-driving chip or fsd  in 2019 which is the basis for the hw  3.0 chipset used in the current models  of tesla cars the fsd packs in 6 billion  transistors and includes an integrated  neural network processor gpu safety  systems and security system for the  later models of the fsd samsung provided  the system on a chip or soc which is  essentially the entire integrated  circuit or ic around the chip this was a  major upgrade from tesla's previous  nvidia chips offering 21 times greater  performance in a smaller footprint this  upgrade by samsung has played an  important role in reducing costs while  maintaining the performance and range of  newer generation tesla cars now in 2021  tesla's internal chip development team  has come up with a new model called the  d1 or dojo chip and samsung will again  help tesla manufacture these newer  generations of chips and socs the d1  processor packs a whopping 50 billion  transistors and delivers 362 teraflops  of power it is an application specific  integrated circuit or asic built upon  samsung's 7 nanometer node technology to  be clear the d1 chip in its current form  will not be used in the final production  cars their purpose is twofold first they  will be used in massive networks to  train machine learning models within  tesla which will form the basis of the  new tesla vision system software and  neural network and second their  technology will be used as a blueprint  by samsung to manufacture the hw 4.0  chips which will be mounted in the new  tesla car models and run the vision  system software to self-drive the cars  in a nutshell tesla in collaboration  with samsung has managed to create the  most powerful supercomputer solely  dedicated to training a neural network  that will make self-driving cars a  reality on the road soon people in the  industry are already touting the d1  chips as a game changer in computing  performance and their ability to train  large neural networks is second to none  the way these supercomputers work is 354  connected neural training nodes make a  d1 chip 25 connected d1 chips make a  training tile 12 training tiles makes a  cabinet and 10 cabinets make the exopod  which is the name of this supercomputer  exopod has the capability of providing  1.1 e-flaps which is 1100 teraflops for  processing power which is an insane  amount plus its high bandwidth low  latency architecture allows it to  perform four times better than any other  ai supercomputer at the same cost while  keeping the carbon footprint five times  smaller and saving more energy this  massive amount of processing power is  crucial to rapidly training tesla's ai  neural networks which will eventually  end up driving the new generation of  cars from 2022 onwards think of exopod  as an ascent hive mind that when trained  properly can reach a level of autonomy  where it can constantly communicate with  all tesla cars all over the globe  helping them navigate the streets while  you relax in your seat not just that the  great thing about machine learning and  neural networks is that it is a  perpetual learning loop so at the same  time as it is helping cars around the  world it is also absorbing vast sums of  data from these cars to build up its  knowledge even further with this  collaboration with samsung it seems that  elon is well on his way to making that a  reality fulfilling the promise of fully  self-driving cars on the road maybe even  before the end of this decade now in all  honesty this is just the start of the  association and it will still take years  to realize that dream but nonetheless  the new samsung manufactured tesla h 4.0  chip which will most likely get mounted  into the new cyber truck is an  exponential jump in performance that is  bound to come with some unique features  that we haven't seen in other tesla  models yet i for one cannot wait to see  what they are and what elon and tesla  have in store for us next we will keep  following the story as it unfolds so  make sure you subscribe to the channel  and ring the notification bell to get  notified the next time we release  another video and if you are a huge fan  of elon and tesla just like us smash  that like button and share some of that  love our way as well till then from all  of us here at simply tech have a great  day ahead and see you in the next video
 

